## Deploy

After CC commits and CI image rebuild:

````bash
# On agent-01
cd /opt/hp1-agent
git pull origin main

# .env is unchanged from v2.49.5 — POSTGRES_PASSWORD with $$$$ stays
cd docker
docker compose --env-file .env --profile pgbouncer up -d --force-recreate pgbouncer

# Verify the container env now has DATABASE_URL empty
docker exec hp1_pgbouncer env | grep -E '^(DATABASE_URL|DATABASE_URLS|DB_)'
# Should show DATABASE_URL= (empty), DATABASE_URLS= (empty), and the DB_* set.

# Userlist should now have LITERAL password (no %25, no %24)
docker exec hp1_pgbouncer cat /etc/pgbouncer/userlist.txt

docker compose ps pgbouncer
# Expect (healthy)

# Real upstream auth — should return 1 row
docker exec -e PGPASSWORD='Jw%ZY%F$$Bz2Fn2L' hp1_pgbouncer \
  psql -h /var/run/pgbouncer -p 6432 -U hp1 -d hp1_agent -c 'SELECT 1;'
````

If `SELECT 1;` returns one row, both SCRAM legs work and the
front-side flip for hp1_agent (`DATABASE_URL` to socket form) is the
next operator step.


